threads.body:
@copilot Update this existing PR directly to revise the context-scoping guidance. The user has reconsidered the original before-send rule. Application request-generation hooks and response-consumption callbacks are symmetric: both can contribute to the exchange without their application work belonging under the outgoing CLIENT or PRODUCER span. The agreed direction is captured caller context for application callbacks in both directions, with operation context scoped to justified library-internal execution rather than every request/before-send hook. Classify by the code being invoked, not request versus response or before versus after timing.

Revise .github/agents/knowledge/instrumentation-context-scoping.md accordingly and keep its index entry accurate. Preserve the distinction between asynchronous span lifetime and thread-bound Scope lifetime, restoring the full captured caller Context including span-free contexts, scope restoration after callbacks, and correct remote outgoing-span propagation. Do not imply CLIENT/PRODUCER spans must be leaves or remove justified internal contexts and duplicate-span suppression. Do not require ending an operation before every callback; retain correct terminal completion behavior without prematurely ending request or response processing. Preserve explicit application context choices. Explain that independently instrumented outgoing work started by application callbacks must not be accidentally suppressed or parented to the enclosing outgoing span.

Include focused testing guidance for application request/body generation, response consumption including deferred demand, completion, failure, inline/asynchronous execution, no caller span, custom Context values, and restoration of an unrelated callback thread's context. Keep the article concise and avoid prescribing unverified framework-specific behavior. The full repository-wide audit is still outstanding and tracked in #20958; updating this guidance is not completion of that audit and must not close that issue. Do not update any other PR or perform the full audit. Follow the repository's documentation tooling when applicable. Acceptance is revised, symmetric guidance with the useful lifecycle/internal-execution distinctions retained. This request supersedes this PR's original blanket before-send context convention.
